Z||000006||2xsess||12-01-2001||09:03 AM||||Jimmy, how much work was it to get those fastback taillights into the notchback? How did you do it? <P><BR>Sweet Fieros <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">           <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||jimmybpei||12-01-2001||09:15 AM||||really not that much work. first i just cut the rear quaters off and then ground the quaters about 6" to foot back and then made a shapped template to lay inside the quaters to hold the fiberglas in place whil it set up.<P>Then i cut the quaters to length and started shaping them. Once that wa done i fitted the tails in. had to make a new mounting bracket to hold them into place.<P>Than it was onto extending the trunk and fitting that. <P>i did this car about 6 years ago and the quaters havent cracked yet. i usually keep the trunk closed at car shows 'cause it dosn't look too pretty in there. Will take some pics today and post them.<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B.||||reg||1
Z||000008||TRiAD||12-01-2001||10:47 AM||||How'd you do the covers over the front signals? I like!!!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroRacer||12-01-2001||12:00 PM||||Really slick cars, I also like the clear taillights!!  If I get Fiero number two in january, I may do something like that to it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||jimmybpei||12-01-2001||12:44 PM||||OK guys here are a few pics of the inside of the trunk. Carfull thay arn't too pretty, i may try to finish up this winter if time permits.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/yell-dr.tail.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/yell-tails.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/yel-trunk.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/yel-dr.quater.jpg"> <P>Thats about as good as ican show it.<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B.<P>||||reg||1
